---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Legal" description="ShelfBee privacy policy and terms of service.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Privacy &amp; terms</h1>
      <p class="sub">How ShelfBee handles your data, and the terms for using the extension.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="card" id="privacy">
      <h2>Privacy policy</h2>
      <p class="meta">Effective date: July 1, 2025 &nbsp;·&nbsp; Last updated: July 2025</p>

      <div class="summary">
        <p><strong>The short version:</strong> ShelfBee does not collect, store, or transmit any personal data. Library availability lookups happen directly between your device and your library's servers. We have no backend, no analytics, and no accounts. Your reading habits stay yours.</p>
      </div>

      <h3>Who we are</h3>
      <p>ShelfBee ("we," "us," or "our") is a Safari Web Extension for iOS, iPadOS, and macOS, distributed through the Apple App Store. Questions can be sent to <a href="mailto:support@shelfbee.app">support@shelfbee.app</a>.</p>

      <h3>Information we do not collect</h3>
      <p>We do not collect, store, or process:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your name, email address, or any account information</li>
        <li>The books you browse or search</li>
        <li>Your library card number or library account credentials</li>
        <li>Your device identifiers or IP address</li>
        <li>Location data</li>
        <li>Browsing history</li>
        <li>Usage analytics or crash reports sent to us</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>How library lookups work</h3>
      <p>When you visit a supported book page, ShelfBee reads the page's book metadata (such as title and ISBN) and uses it to query your library's availability data via OverDrive/Libby's public endpoints. This request goes from your device directly to those services — it does not pass through any ShelfBee server, because we don't operate one.</p>
      <p>Your chosen library is saved locally on your device using standard iOS/macOS system storage (UserDefaults and App Groups). This data never leaves your device.</p>

      <h3>Pages we can read</h3>
      <p>ShelfBee requests permission to read page content only on the specific websites it supports (such as Amazon and Goodreads). It reads book metadata only — not your account information, purchase history, or any other page content.</p>

      <h3>Third-party services</h3>
      <p>When ShelfBee performs a library availability check, your device communicates directly with OverDrive/Libby servers. That communication is governed by <a href="https://company.overdrive.com/company/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OverDrive's privacy policy</a>, not ours.</p>
      <p>We do not use any third-party analytics SDKs, advertising networks, or tracking services in the app.</p>

      <h3>Support correspondence</h3>
      <p>If you contact us at <a href="mailto:support@shelfbee.app">support@shelfbee.app</a>, we receive and read your email. We use this only to respond to your inquiry and do not store it in any external system beyond our email inbox. We do not share support correspondence with third parties.</p>

      <h3>Children's privacy</h3>
      <p>ShelfBee does not knowingly collect any information from children under 13. The app contains no features that require personal data from any user.</p>

      <h3>Changes to this policy</h3>
      <p>If we ever change how the app handles data in a meaningful way, we will update this page and revise the effective date above. Continued use of the app after changes constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.</p>

      <h3>Contact</h3>
      <p>Questions or concerns about privacy? Email us at <a href="mailto:support@shelfbee.app">support@shelfbee.app</a>. We'll respond within 48 hours on business days.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="card" id="terms">
      <h2>Terms of service</h2>
      <p class="meta">Effective date: July 1, 2026 &nbsp;·&nbsp; Last updated: July 2026</p>

      <p>By downloading or using ShelfBee ("the app" or "the extension"), you agree to these terms. If you don't agree, please don't use the app.</p>

      <h3>What ShelfBee does</h3>
      <p>ShelfBee is a Safari Web Extension that checks library availability for books on supported websites. It is intended for personal, non-commercial use. Library availability data is sourced from OverDrive/Libby and may not always be current or accurate.</p>

      <h3>What you can do</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Install and use ShelfBee on devices you own or control</li>
        <li>Use it to check book availability at participating libraries</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>What you can't do</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Reverse engineer, decompile, or modify the app</li>
        <li>Use the app to scrape or aggregate library availability data at scale</li>
        <li>Redistribute or resell the app</li>
        <li>Use the app for any unlawful purpose</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Library relationships</h3>
      <p>ShelfBee is an independent app and is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or partnered with OverDrive, Libby, Amazon, Goodreads, or any public library system. Your relationship with your library — including borrowing, holds, and account access — is governed entirely by your library's own policies.</p>

      <h3>Availability and accuracy</h3>
      <p>We make no guarantee that the app will be available at all times or that library availability information will be accurate. Library catalogs update independently and there may be a delay between actual availability and what ShelfBee shows.</p>

      <h3>Disclaimer of warranties</h3>
      <p>ShelfBee is provided "as is," without warranty of any kind, express or implied. We do not warrant that the app will be error-free or uninterrupted.</p>

      <h3>Limitation of liability</h3>
      <p>To the fullest extent permitted by law, ShelfBee and its developer shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, or consequential damages arising from your use of the app.</p>

      <h3>Changes to these terms</h3>
      <p>We may update these terms from time to time. Continued use of the app after changes are posted constitutes your acceptance of the new terms. We'll update the effective date above when we do.</p>

      <h3>Governing law</h3>
      <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the United States and the state of Colorado, without regard to conflict of law provisions.</p>

      <h3>Contact</h3>
      <p>Questions about these terms? Email <a href="mailto:support@shelfbee.app">support@shelfbee.app</a>.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .wrap {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 20px 40px 60px;
  }

  .page-head {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-label);
    color: var(--brand-tan);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: var(--fs-title);
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0 0 10px;
    font-weight: var(--fw-bold);
  }

  .sub {
    font-size: var(--fs-subhead);
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--brand-plum-2);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .card {
    background: #fff;
    border: 1px solid var(--brand-line);
    border-radius: var(--r-card);
    padding: 26px 28px;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
    scroll-margin-top: 24px;
  }

  .card h2 {
    font-size: var(--fs-heading);
    margin: 0 0 6px;
    font-weight: var(--fw-semibold);
    color: var(--brand-plum);
  }

  .meta {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-label);
    color: var(--brand-tan);
    margin: 0 0 20px;
  }

  .summary {
    background: var(--brand-cream-2);
    border: 1px solid var(--brand-line);
    border-radius: var(--r-lg);
    padding: 16px 18px;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }

  .summary p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--brand-plum-2);
  }

  .summary strong {
    color: var(--brand-plum);
    font-weight: var(--fw-semibold);
  }

  .card h3 {
    font-size: var(--fs-subhead);
    color: var(--brand-plum);
    font-weight: var(--fw-semibold);
    margin: 24px 0 8px;
  }

  .card p {
    font-size: var(--fs-body);
    line-height: var(--lh-relaxed);
    color: var(--brand-plum-2);
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }

  .card ul {
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    padding-left: 20px;
  }

  .card ul li {
    font-size: var(--fs-body);
    line-height: var(--lh-relaxed);
    color: var(--brand-plum-2);
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }

  .card a {
    color: var(--brand-sunset-2);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .card a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .wrap {
      padding: 20px 20px 40px;
    }
  }
</style>
